1
00:00:11,220 --> 00:00:12,930
♪

2
00:00:13,013 --> 00:00:14,473
[NARRATOR] In the near future,

3
00:00:14,556 --> 00:00:16,892
the e-Pulse generated
by human thoughts and emotions

4
00:00:16,975 --> 00:00:19,937
is the energy source
for a new line of AI devices

5
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:21,396
called "Sapotamas,"

6
00:00:21,480 --> 00:00:24,191
a giant technological advance
for humanity.

7
00:00:24,858 --> 00:00:26,526
But from this giant's shadow,

8
00:00:26,610 --> 00:00:28,487
frightening monsters emerge,

9
00:00:28,570 --> 00:00:31,281
monsters that evolve
by consuming e-Pulse.

10
00:00:31,365 --> 00:00:32,783
They are known as...

11
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:35,661
[♪ opening theme song playing]

12
00:01:56,908 --> 00:02:00,078
[Tomoro breathing shakily]

13
00:02:08,837 --> 00:02:11,757
-Murasamemon, are you good?
-I am.

14
00:02:12,507 --> 00:02:13,592
[Tomoro breathing weakly]

15
00:02:14,551 --> 00:02:16,887
[MURASAMEMON]
Hurry, while the rift is open.

16
00:02:16,970 --> 00:02:18,180
It won't last long.

17
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:20,390
[Reina groans]

18
00:02:21,391 --> 00:02:22,392
[TOMORO] Are you okay?

19
00:02:24,102 --> 00:02:26,355
[Tomoro panting]

20
00:02:34,029 --> 00:02:36,281
[Tomoro weakly] A... suka.

21
00:02:36,365 --> 00:02:37,240
[gasps]

22
00:02:43,538 --> 00:02:44,456
[grunts softly]

23
00:02:44,539 --> 00:02:47,000
[Kekomon snoring]

24
00:02:49,252 --> 00:02:52,673
[Reina sobbing]

25
00:02:58,095 --> 00:02:59,513
You're all okay.

26
00:02:59,596 --> 00:03:01,348
That's the important thing.

27
00:03:02,265 --> 00:03:05,394
-[REINA] But Murasamemon's gone.
-[Tomoro gasps]

28
00:03:07,396 --> 00:03:09,481
[Reina continues sobbing]

29
00:03:09,564 --> 00:03:12,734
Murasamemon
made that sacrifice...

30
00:03:14,569 --> 00:03:17,155
...for our sake,
the family's sake.

31
00:03:17,239 --> 00:03:19,533
[Reina continues sobbing]

32
00:03:21,076 --> 00:03:22,077
[groans]

33
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:24,579
[Reina continues sobbing]

34
00:03:25,247 --> 00:03:27,874
[YOSHIMURA] Don't push yourself.
Get some sleep.

35
00:03:35,090 --> 00:03:37,050
[static hissing]

36
00:03:47,269 --> 00:03:49,479
-[all exclaiming]
-Keko.

37
00:03:51,189 --> 00:03:52,232
[TOMORO] How is Kyo?

38
00:03:52,983 --> 00:03:53,942
[YOSHIMURA] Uh...

39
00:03:54,818 --> 00:03:56,486
Well, he'll live,

40
00:03:56,570 --> 00:03:58,613
just not as a Cleaner.

41
00:03:59,281 --> 00:04:01,116
[TOMORO] What happened
to Murasamemon...

42
00:04:02,701 --> 00:04:03,785
...it was my fault.

43
00:04:05,579 --> 00:04:07,372
-[ERYNGII] Emergency!
-Huh?

44
00:04:07,456 --> 00:04:09,666
-Come see who's on TV.
-[YOSHIMURA] Huh?

45
00:04:10,625 --> 00:04:13,378
[CHAIRMAN WONG] The anomaly
was only recently discovered.

46
00:04:13,462 --> 00:04:16,965
People who emit
an abnormal or unstable e-Pulse

47
00:04:17,048 --> 00:04:19,593
can cause
an unforeseen error to occur,

48
00:04:19,676 --> 00:04:21,762
a glitch in their Sapotama.

49
00:04:22,345 --> 00:04:24,389
This glitch
is capable of producing

50
00:04:24,473 --> 00:04:27,350
-a breed of monster, Digimon.
-[gasps]

51
00:04:27,434 --> 00:04:28,518
♪

52
00:04:29,144 --> 00:04:31,438
[CHAIRMAN WONG] The existence
of these Digimon was hidden,

53
00:04:31,521 --> 00:04:33,815
kept secret
from the World Union.

54
00:04:33,899 --> 00:04:35,692
The Ministry of Civil Protection

55
00:04:35,776 --> 00:04:38,069
used a gang of criminals
called Cleaners

56
00:04:38,153 --> 00:04:41,531
to cover this up
so no one would find out.

57
00:04:41,615 --> 00:04:42,949
But not to worry.

58
00:04:43,033 --> 00:04:44,326
I'm happy to report that

59
00:04:44,409 --> 00:04:47,370
we have completely debugged
all Sapotamas,

60
00:04:47,454 --> 00:04:49,247
and now,
we're going to update them

61
00:04:49,331 --> 00:04:51,166
to a brand-new system.

62
00:04:51,791 --> 00:04:52,918
These new Sapotamas

63
00:04:53,210 --> 00:04:55,253
will automatically link
with their owners.

64
00:04:55,337 --> 00:04:58,131
Thanks to their updated systems,
they'll be able to detect

65
00:04:58,215 --> 00:05:00,467
any abnormal
e-Pulse fluctuations

66
00:05:00,550 --> 00:05:02,260
well in advance,

67
00:05:02,344 --> 00:05:06,431
and thereby preemptively remove
the Digimon-creating glitch.

68
00:05:06,515 --> 00:05:08,266
-[beeping]
-[MAN 1] Huh?

69
00:05:08,350 --> 00:05:10,936
[MAN 2] It's already
started updating.

70
00:05:11,019 --> 00:05:13,355
-Huh?
-[WOMAN 1] Guess it's updating.

71
00:05:13,438 --> 00:05:15,440
[indistinct chatter]

72
00:05:19,486 --> 00:05:20,403
Huh?

73
00:05:20,487 --> 00:05:22,197
[SAPOTAMA] Update completed.

74
00:05:22,280 --> 00:05:24,741
Automatically linking now.

75
00:05:25,450 --> 00:05:28,203
This will prevent any further
glitches from happening.

76
00:05:28,787 --> 00:05:31,331
We can then bring these Digimon
out into the open

77
00:05:31,414 --> 00:05:33,458
and properly manage them,

78
00:05:33,542 --> 00:05:37,170
bringing us one step closer
to the ideal world we all want.

79
00:05:39,297 --> 00:05:41,841
I think we can all agree
this is wonderful news.

80
00:05:41,925 --> 00:05:44,010
Hold on! I completely disagree!

81
00:05:44,094 --> 00:05:46,555
Discriminating against people
based on their e-Pulse,

82
00:05:46,638 --> 00:05:48,181
-I think that's outrageous!
-[beeping]

83
00:05:48,265 --> 00:05:51,226
-Huh?
-Abnormal e-Pulse detected.

84
00:05:51,309 --> 00:05:54,020
Possible Digimon creation
anticipated.

85
00:05:54,104 --> 00:05:55,480
Removing glitch now.

86
00:05:56,731 --> 00:05:58,692
Huh? Oh.

87
00:05:58,775 --> 00:06:00,652
[screams]

88
00:06:00,735 --> 00:06:02,362
[screaming]

89
00:06:05,323 --> 00:06:06,575
[indistinct chatter]

90
00:06:06,658 --> 00:06:07,659
[HITOMI] That must mean
there was a glitch

91
00:06:07,742 --> 00:06:09,035
in his e-Pulse.

92
00:06:10,161 --> 00:06:13,039
But wait, something's not right
about this.

93
00:06:13,123 --> 00:06:14,332
I mean...

94
00:06:14,416 --> 00:06:15,917
-[beeping]
- [gasps]

95
00:06:16,001 --> 00:06:18,169
[SAPOTAMA]
E-Pulse fluctuation detected.

96
00:06:18,795 --> 00:06:20,505
-Take a deep breath.
-Huh?

97
00:06:22,966 --> 00:06:24,926
This is simply astounding.

98
00:06:25,010 --> 00:06:26,511
Yes. As you can see,

99
00:06:26,595 --> 00:06:29,139
everything lies
in Chairman Wong's hands now.

100
00:06:29,848 --> 00:06:31,099
-[portal hums open]
-[GENJO] Huh?

101
00:06:31,182 --> 00:06:33,310
What in the world is going on?

102
00:06:33,393 --> 00:06:35,228
How are you able
to Cold Heart people

103
00:06:35,312 --> 00:06:36,563
without a Digimon?

104
00:06:37,731 --> 00:06:38,898
[GENJO] By taking advantage

105
00:06:38,982 --> 00:06:41,735
of one of Albatusmon's
unique capabilities.

106
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:43,778
All Sapotamas in the world

107
00:06:43,862 --> 00:06:46,239
are in constant,
continuous connection

108
00:06:46,323 --> 00:06:49,367
with the Apraxas,
the Mirror World host server.

109
00:06:50,035 --> 00:06:52,078
They can't be
disconnected from it.

110
00:06:54,039 --> 00:06:57,459
And we've placed Albatusmon
within the server's core.

111
00:06:59,085 --> 00:07:02,088
When a Sapotama
detects an abnormal e-Pulse,

112
00:07:02,172 --> 00:07:04,049
it makes use of
Albatusmon's ability

113
00:07:04,132 --> 00:07:06,468
to endlessly drain e-Pulse.

114
00:07:06,551 --> 00:07:08,553
-[SAPOTAMA] Removing glitch now.
-[woman gasps]

115
00:07:08,637 --> 00:07:10,347
-No! [grunts]
-[gasps]

116
00:07:10,430 --> 00:07:13,099
[GENJO] The e-Pulse is drained
from the Sapotama's linked owner

117
00:07:13,183 --> 00:07:15,518
by way of their implants tag,

118
00:07:15,602 --> 00:07:17,938
and then transmitted
to Albatusmon.

119
00:07:18,897 --> 00:07:21,775
Hmm. So now you can
Cold Heart at will

120
00:07:21,858 --> 00:07:24,819
anyone, anywhere on the planet
who owns a Sapotama

121
00:07:24,903 --> 00:07:26,321
based on your selection.

122
00:07:28,323 --> 00:07:30,408
[chuckles] From now on,

123
00:07:30,492 --> 00:07:34,621
I will be the one who controls
the creation of all Digimon.

124
00:07:34,704 --> 00:07:38,166
I will be dictating the rules
like an all-powerful god.

125
00:07:38,917 --> 00:07:41,711
So that's your
Shangri-La Project.

126
00:07:41,795 --> 00:07:44,422
The one remaining issue
is the Cleaners.

127
00:07:45,131 --> 00:07:48,134
Their Sapotamas function
differently than all the others,

128
00:07:48,218 --> 00:07:50,929
which means they're not
connected to the Apraxas.

129
00:07:51,596 --> 00:07:55,850
[CHAIRMAN WONG] Rose Woodville,
you will eliminate the Cleaners.

130
00:07:56,518 --> 00:07:57,435
[sighs]

131
00:07:59,979 --> 00:08:02,273
The other two asked me
to turn these in.

132
00:08:02,357 --> 00:08:04,067
Fire and Water.

133
00:08:04,150 --> 00:08:06,403
You mean to say
they're quitting the Five Stars?

134
00:08:06,486 --> 00:08:09,197
That's right. And here's mine
while we're at it.

135
00:08:09,280 --> 00:08:10,365
[clinking]

136
00:08:14,327 --> 00:08:15,453
[CHAIRMAN WONG] Hmm.

137
00:08:15,537 --> 00:08:17,247
There's nothing to worry about.

138
00:08:17,330 --> 00:08:18,832
I anticipated this,

139
00:08:18,915 --> 00:08:21,626
so I've already
dispatched the new Star of Wood.

140
00:08:23,503 --> 00:08:24,546
[RAITO] Kaito.

141
00:08:25,380 --> 00:08:26,464
What are you saying?

142
00:08:26,548 --> 00:08:29,300
I'm saying I'm not
a Five Star anymore.

143
00:08:29,384 --> 00:08:30,844
You're on your own, kid.

144
00:08:32,637 --> 00:08:33,680
-Five Star or not...
-Huh?

145
00:08:33,972 --> 00:08:36,516
...I'll follow you to the end,
Kaito. Wait up!

146
00:08:36,599 --> 00:08:37,684
Huh?

147
00:08:44,441 --> 00:08:46,526
So what now? What do we do?

148
00:08:46,609 --> 00:08:48,695
We don't have Digimon criminals
to hunt down.

149
00:08:48,778 --> 00:08:50,238
Kyo is out of commission.

150
00:08:50,864 --> 00:08:53,491
Let's face it,
there's nothing we can do.

151
00:08:53,575 --> 00:08:54,743
You're just gonna quit

152
00:08:54,826 --> 00:08:57,287
and let these guys
do whatever they please?

153
00:08:57,370 --> 00:08:59,789
We were never heroes.
We just had a job to do.

154
00:08:59,873 --> 00:09:00,915
Keko.

155
00:09:01,916 --> 00:09:03,168
Yeah, I know.

156
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:05,920
I wanna get Asuka back, too.

157
00:09:06,004 --> 00:09:07,380
Keko, keko.

158
00:09:07,464 --> 00:09:08,631
But I know...

159
00:09:08,965 --> 00:09:11,134
[voice breaking] I know that
it's all 'cause of me...

160
00:09:11,885 --> 00:09:13,970
that Kyo and Murasamemon...

161
00:09:15,847 --> 00:09:16,765
Keko.

162
00:09:18,349 --> 00:09:19,476
[grunts softly]

163
00:09:20,268 --> 00:09:22,103
-[explosion]
-[rumbling]

164
00:09:22,187 --> 00:09:24,439
Big trouble, you guys,
and I do mean big!

165
00:09:24,522 --> 00:09:25,774
-[ALL] Huh?
-[glass shattering]

166
00:09:33,990 --> 00:09:36,576
[woman cackling wickedly]

167
00:09:36,659 --> 00:09:39,496
Come on out here and say hello
to the newest Five Star,

168
00:09:39,579 --> 00:09:41,247
Senka Paradise!

169
00:09:41,331 --> 00:09:43,249
Cleaners!

170
00:09:43,917 --> 00:09:45,376
Ready to play?

171
00:09:51,466 --> 00:09:54,803
[MAKI] The Ministry of Civil
Protection Special Ward.

172
00:09:54,886 --> 00:09:56,137
What do you keep in here?

173
00:09:56,221 --> 00:09:58,181
We lost contact with HQ.

174
00:09:58,264 --> 00:10:00,016
-I think we should-- Huh?
-[gasps]

175
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:02,143
[SAPOTAMA]
Abnormal e-Pulse detected.

176
00:10:02,227 --> 00:10:04,187
-[screams]
-[men whimper]

177
00:10:04,270 --> 00:10:06,481
-[SAPOTAMA] Removing glitch now.
-[screams]

178
00:10:06,564 --> 00:10:07,690
-[grunts angrily]
-[thuds]

179
00:10:07,774 --> 00:10:09,234
[KAWARAZAKI] This way. Hurry.

180
00:10:10,026 --> 00:10:11,027
So that's it.

181
00:10:11,319 --> 00:10:12,862
First, they use the Ministry
as a scapegoat,

182
00:10:12,946 --> 00:10:14,239
and then they silence you.

183
00:10:14,864 --> 00:10:16,032
They'll get to me soon,

184
00:10:16,115 --> 00:10:17,116
but there's someone
I need you to meet

185
00:10:17,200 --> 00:10:18,618
while I still have time.

186
00:10:21,663 --> 00:10:23,581
-[door opens]
-[MIHARU] Hmm?

187
00:10:24,374 --> 00:10:26,334
Well, Dr. Tenma, is it ready?

188
00:10:27,210 --> 00:10:29,587
I could only formulate
a small amount.

189
00:10:29,671 --> 00:10:32,298
It won't be enough.
Show them, Miharu.

190
00:10:32,382 --> 00:10:33,258
[MIHARU] Right.

191
00:10:35,885 --> 00:10:38,137
This spray will disconnect
your implant tag

192
00:10:38,221 --> 00:10:39,556
from your Sapotama.

193
00:10:40,682 --> 00:10:41,808
[electricity crackling]

194
00:10:44,102 --> 00:10:47,438
-Weren't you with GIFT?
-Hmm.

195
00:10:48,106 --> 00:10:50,483
And if your name is Tenma,
does that mean...

196
00:10:50,567 --> 00:10:51,568
[pulsing]

197
00:10:51,651 --> 00:10:53,528
[SAPOTAMA]
Abnormal e-Pulse detected.

198
00:10:54,070 --> 00:10:56,698
Give me your hand.
There isn't much left, but...

199
00:10:57,615 --> 00:10:59,784
-Huh?
-[SAPOTAMA] Removing glitch now.

200
00:11:02,787 --> 00:11:04,038
My time is up.

201
00:11:04,747 --> 00:11:06,082
Listen, Maki,

202
00:11:06,666 --> 00:11:08,459
I have a request.

203
00:11:08,543 --> 00:11:10,169
Please deliver this spray

204
00:11:10,962 --> 00:11:13,590
and Dr. Tenma
to the Glowing Dawn

205
00:11:13,673 --> 00:11:16,259
-before it's too late.
-Kawarazaki!

206
00:11:17,010 --> 00:11:18,052
Find them.

207
00:11:18,678 --> 00:11:21,931
They'll need all the help...
they can get.

208
00:11:22,599 --> 00:11:25,476
And then give them this,

209
00:11:25,560 --> 00:11:28,188
[straining]
my last job for them.

210
00:11:32,275 --> 00:11:34,027
♪

211
00:11:34,777 --> 00:11:35,820
[TOMORO] Who are these guys?

212
00:11:36,237 --> 00:11:39,073
[CHIROPMON] Brachiomon,
Vermillimon, and Triceramon.

213
00:11:39,157 --> 00:11:40,241
They're Ultimate Digimon,

214
00:11:40,325 --> 00:11:42,118
and they're seriously
overloading.

215
00:11:42,202 --> 00:11:43,661
Like what happened
with Gogmamon.

216
00:11:43,745 --> 00:11:47,665
[cackles] All right, guys,
let the Cleaner hunt begin.

217
00:11:47,749 --> 00:11:49,751
Shouldn't you be trying
to run away or something?

218
00:11:49,834 --> 00:11:51,753
You really think
you can take us down?

219
00:11:51,836 --> 00:11:53,087
Not gonna happen!

220
00:11:54,464 --> 00:11:55,882
-[grunts]
-[screams]

221
00:11:56,883 --> 00:11:58,259
[gasps] Pristimon!

222
00:11:59,928 --> 00:12:01,846
[CHIROPMON] Condense Dazzle!

223
00:12:01,930 --> 00:12:04,182
-Oh!
-[MAKOTO] Chiropmon!

224
00:12:04,265 --> 00:12:06,142
[Senka cackling]

225
00:12:06,226 --> 00:12:07,685
-[grunts]
-[KEKOMON] Keko!

226
00:12:13,900 --> 00:12:15,443
Oh, Gekkomon.

227
00:12:15,526 --> 00:12:17,946
Mess with Tomoro
and you mess with me, you know?

228
00:12:20,073 --> 00:12:22,200
Swing Tackle!

229
00:12:22,283 --> 00:12:24,243
-[gurgling]
-[grunts]

230
00:12:24,327 --> 00:12:25,703
Huh?

231
00:12:25,787 --> 00:12:28,206
[Gekkomon babbling]

232
00:12:28,289 --> 00:12:30,041
[panting]

233
00:12:30,124 --> 00:12:32,335
Tomoro, time to Digivolve,
you know?

234
00:12:32,418 --> 00:12:35,046
Uh. [grunting]

235
00:12:35,672 --> 00:12:37,340
Hey, what is it? What's wrong?

236
00:12:37,423 --> 00:12:40,218
I'm, like, not feeling
your beat at all, you know.

237
00:12:40,301 --> 00:12:41,719
[quivering]

238
00:12:42,512 --> 00:12:43,805
-[sighs in defeat]
-[GEKKOMON] Oh.

239
00:12:45,807 --> 00:12:47,141
[TOMORO] What's the point?

240
00:12:53,523 --> 00:12:56,901
What are we...
What are we even fighting for?

241
00:12:56,985 --> 00:12:58,820
-Mm.
-[gulps]

242
00:12:58,903 --> 00:13:01,823
[laughs boisterously]
I don't know about you,

243
00:13:01,906 --> 00:13:04,784
but I'm here because you people
are wanted criminals.

244
00:13:04,867 --> 00:13:08,621
You're all a bunch of glitches,
and glitches get removed.

245
00:13:08,705 --> 00:13:11,541
[growls]

246
00:13:11,624 --> 00:13:14,377
I bet... Kyo would know
what to do right now.

247
00:13:15,420 --> 00:13:17,922
He would. He always did.

248
00:13:18,798 --> 00:13:20,466
[KYO] Sorry to keep
everyone waiting.

249
00:13:22,135 --> 00:13:23,386
Are you ready?

250
00:13:28,141 --> 00:13:29,267
-[loud thud]
-[gasps]

251
00:13:29,350 --> 00:13:32,020
[Senka cackles maliciously]

252
00:13:32,103 --> 00:13:33,146
Bye-bye now.

253
00:13:33,229 --> 00:13:35,314
[TIALUDOMON] Frisbicker!

254
00:13:35,398 --> 00:13:37,358
[roars]

255
00:13:38,109 --> 00:13:39,652
What the heck's going on?

256
00:13:42,071 --> 00:13:44,490
Hotaruko. Why is she--

257
00:13:44,574 --> 00:13:46,617
[Yoshimura chuckles]
I made a couple of calls.

258
00:13:46,701 --> 00:13:49,454
I figured you needed
all the friends you can get.

259
00:13:49,537 --> 00:13:52,540
[SENKA] Former members
of Tactics, huh? Perfect.

260
00:13:52,623 --> 00:13:55,168
Saves me the trouble
of hunting you down, too.

261
00:13:55,251 --> 00:13:58,004
I think you'll find
you're the one being hunted.

262
00:13:58,087 --> 00:14:01,674
-[yells]
-[roars]

263
00:14:04,177 --> 00:14:05,845
[grunts] Granit! [gasps]

264
00:14:10,391 --> 00:14:11,392
[grunts]

265
00:14:12,602 --> 00:14:13,895
You okay, Ludomon?

266
00:14:14,479 --> 00:14:15,897
[Hotaruko screams]

267
00:14:20,693 --> 00:14:22,737
Hotaruko, this is just crazy.

268
00:14:22,820 --> 00:14:24,781
You're up against
Ultimate Digimon.

269
00:14:25,406 --> 00:14:28,242
Even so, we're still
going to protect you.

270
00:14:28,326 --> 00:14:30,161
-Huh?
-Hmm.

271
00:14:30,244 --> 00:14:32,747
This time it's our turn
to help you out.

272
00:14:32,830 --> 00:14:35,374
-Thank you, Granit.
-[growls]

273
00:14:35,458 --> 00:14:38,336
Like, crap. Empty words
from a bunch of scrubs

274
00:14:38,419 --> 00:14:40,046
who are about to be-- [grunts]

275
00:14:40,129 --> 00:14:41,881
[Petitmon shrieks]

276
00:14:44,175 --> 00:14:45,510
You guys.

277
00:14:47,637 --> 00:14:48,679
[grunts]

278
00:14:49,263 --> 00:14:51,974
I don't know what the heck
all of you dimwits are thinking.

279
00:14:52,058 --> 00:14:55,561
What Digimon in its right mind
sides with humans anyway?

280
00:14:55,645 --> 00:14:58,064
You're really gonna
protect these glitches?

281
00:14:58,898 --> 00:14:59,982
Poyo, poyo.

282
00:15:00,358 --> 00:15:03,236
Huh? You've been living
with these glitches so long,

283
00:15:03,319 --> 00:15:05,738
you've probably
caught the glitch bug yourself.

284
00:15:05,822 --> 00:15:07,573
You've got a wittle fever.

285
00:15:07,657 --> 00:15:09,534
[cackling]

286
00:15:09,617 --> 00:15:11,786
-[whimpers] Huh?
-Nyoki.

287
00:15:11,869 --> 00:15:13,663
[ERYNGII] What's wrong
with being a glitch?

288
00:15:13,746 --> 00:15:15,039
[SENKA] Uh?

289
00:15:15,123 --> 00:15:16,207
[grunts]

290
00:15:16,290 --> 00:15:18,501
Okay, now who are you guys?

291
00:15:18,584 --> 00:15:21,754
-[roars]
-[all groan]

292
00:15:21,838 --> 00:15:23,005
[determined grunts]

293
00:15:23,965 --> 00:15:25,341
It's true.

294
00:15:25,424 --> 00:15:29,095
The three of us
used to be completely hopeless.

295
00:15:29,178 --> 00:15:32,432
But then, the man
who made this place told us

296
00:15:33,057 --> 00:15:35,893
that it's never too late
to start over!

297
00:15:36,769 --> 00:15:40,982
Someday, humans and Digimon
will live together in peace.

298
00:15:41,065 --> 00:15:43,734
This place exists
to fulfill that dream,

299
00:15:44,402 --> 00:15:45,653
and that's why

300
00:15:45,736 --> 00:15:47,947
we will never
let you destroy it!

301
00:15:48,030 --> 00:15:49,740
Poison Smash!

302
00:15:50,783 --> 00:15:52,076
Smash!

303
00:15:53,286 --> 00:15:54,954
[grunts]

304
00:15:55,997 --> 00:15:59,083
You can start over,
but a glitch is still a glitch.

305
00:15:59,167 --> 00:16:02,044
Humans and Digimon living
together? [blows raspberry]

306
00:16:02,128 --> 00:16:05,089
I mean, what kind of
worthless dream is that?

307
00:16:05,173 --> 00:16:07,258
Hurry up
and erase these guys already.

308
00:16:07,341 --> 00:16:10,678
-Poyo.
-[SENKA] Bon voyagi. [cackles]

309
00:16:11,471 --> 00:16:12,430
-Gekkomon...
-Chiropmon...

310
00:16:12,722 --> 00:16:14,599
-Pristimon...
-[ALL]...Digivolve to...

311
00:16:31,782 --> 00:16:33,910
...Bearcatmon!

312
00:16:42,877 --> 00:16:45,421
...ScourgeChiropmon!

313
00:16:48,424 --> 00:16:50,968
...Monarchlizamon!

314
00:16:56,682 --> 00:16:58,434
[yelling]

315
00:16:58,518 --> 00:16:59,519
[Senka gasps]

316
00:17:01,812 --> 00:17:03,940
[all screaming]

317
00:17:04,023 --> 00:17:07,068
-[SCOURGECHIROPMON] Gotcha!
-You guys okay? [grunting]

318
00:17:07,151 --> 00:17:08,194
Ugh.

319
00:17:08,277 --> 00:17:09,195
Oh, man,

320
00:17:09,612 --> 00:17:11,489
now you're really starting
to get on my nerves!

321
00:17:13,741 --> 00:17:16,577
[KYO] Glowing Dawn
doesn't delete Digimon.

322
00:17:17,995 --> 00:17:19,705
Does something deserve
to be erased

323
00:17:19,789 --> 00:17:22,208
merely because it's a glitch,
Tomoro?

324
00:17:24,543 --> 00:17:27,171
[TOMORO] Back then,
I couldn't answer him.

325
00:17:28,631 --> 00:17:29,632
But now...

326
00:17:31,092 --> 00:17:32,343
Now I can!

327
00:17:32,802 --> 00:17:34,095
No, it doesn't!

328
00:17:34,178 --> 00:17:35,680
Nothing deserves that!

329
00:17:37,807 --> 00:17:41,102
[KYO] No matter what happens,
don't lose your way.

330
00:17:41,185 --> 00:17:44,605
Trust yourselves,
and trust in your family.

331
00:17:45,731 --> 00:17:46,899
Kyo had a dream,

332
00:17:46,983 --> 00:17:48,985
and we're gonna
make it a reality.

333
00:17:49,068 --> 00:17:50,695
A future where...

334
00:17:50,778 --> 00:17:52,947
Digimon and humans
live together.

335
00:17:53,906 --> 00:17:54,865
What are we?

336
00:17:56,409 --> 00:17:58,619
[ALL] We are the Glowing Dawn!

337
00:18:00,121 --> 00:18:02,456
-[chuckles]
-Hmm.

338
00:18:02,540 --> 00:18:03,916
[light chuckle]

339
00:18:03,999 --> 00:18:05,543
[all chuckling]

340
00:18:05,626 --> 00:18:08,921
-Goodbye, you annoying glitches!
-[roars]

341
00:18:09,005 --> 00:18:11,257
[all yelling]

342
00:18:11,340 --> 00:18:13,926
[SCOURGECHIROPMON]
Despair Blast!

343
00:18:22,935 --> 00:18:26,063
-[grunting]
-[groans]

344
00:18:26,147 --> 00:18:28,649
Murderize Rush!

345
00:18:29,525 --> 00:18:30,484
Hah!

346
00:18:32,445 --> 00:18:33,321
Bubb!

347
00:18:35,406 --> 00:18:38,659
-[MONARCHLIZAMON] Final...
-[roars]

348
00:18:38,743 --> 00:18:41,162
...Judgment!

349
00:18:42,121 --> 00:18:43,914
Go!

350
00:18:47,168 --> 00:18:49,795
[groans]

351
00:18:50,504 --> 00:18:51,505
Poyo!

352
00:18:52,882 --> 00:18:53,883
Oh, well.

353
00:18:53,966 --> 00:18:55,092
That's what I get
for using a bunch

354
00:18:55,176 --> 00:18:56,969
of second-rate Digimon
as back-up.

355
00:18:57,053 --> 00:18:58,596
The next time we do this,

356
00:18:58,679 --> 00:19:01,557
I'll choose better soldiers
from the lab to bring with me.

357
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:03,017
Soldiers?

358
00:19:03,100 --> 00:19:04,393
The next time?

359
00:19:04,477 --> 00:19:06,645
No way. You're going
to the Ministry right now.

360
00:19:06,729 --> 00:19:07,646
-[giggles]
-Uh?

361
00:19:07,730 --> 00:19:09,982
The Ministry
of Civil Protection?

362
00:19:10,066 --> 00:19:11,192
It's already been wiped out.

363
00:19:11,275 --> 00:19:12,985
-It doesn't exist anymore.
-[both gasp]

364
00:19:13,069 --> 00:19:14,403
Who would wipe out the Ministry?

365
00:19:14,487 --> 00:19:17,531
[laughs boisterously]
Sorry, gotta run.

366
00:19:18,449 --> 00:19:19,325
[all gasp]

367
00:19:19,408 --> 00:19:20,993
[Bearcatmon grunts]

368
00:19:22,620 --> 00:19:23,788
[grunts]

369
00:19:24,914 --> 00:19:25,956
Oh.

370
00:19:26,040 --> 00:19:29,126
Hey, guys.
I'm so glad you're all safe.

371
00:19:30,419 --> 00:19:31,629
[YOSHIMURA] Hey!

372
00:19:33,839 --> 00:19:35,466
Miharu, you...

373
00:19:35,549 --> 00:19:36,717
You're okay?

374
00:19:36,801 --> 00:19:37,718
Yes.

375
00:19:38,344 --> 00:19:39,428
Thanks to this.

376
00:19:39,512 --> 00:19:40,971
And I'm hoping
this might be able

377
00:19:41,055 --> 00:19:43,516
to restore Asuka
to the way he was.

378
00:19:43,599 --> 00:19:45,768
-[gasps]
-Excuse me. Who are you?

379
00:19:46,352 --> 00:19:48,187
Dr. Tasuku Tenma.

380
00:19:48,270 --> 00:19:50,439
Tomoro,
this is your grandfather.

381
00:19:50,523 --> 00:19:51,732
[all gasp]

382
00:19:52,191 --> 00:19:53,192
My grandfather.

383
00:19:53,275 --> 00:19:54,985
You don't remember me.

384
00:19:56,362 --> 00:19:58,614
I've caused you all
a great deal of trouble.

385
00:19:59,907 --> 00:20:02,284
After the Kano Island's
disaster,

386
00:20:02,368 --> 00:20:05,496
I protested against
the commercial use of e-Pulse.

387
00:20:06,622 --> 00:20:08,958
Wong did everything he could
to silence me.

388
00:20:09,500 --> 00:20:10,918
He even had
your parents arrested

389
00:20:11,001 --> 00:20:12,837
when they intervened
on my behalf.

390
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:17,216
Thanks to my old college mate,
Yoshi,

391
00:20:17,299 --> 00:20:19,009
as well as Kawarazaki,

392
00:20:19,093 --> 00:20:22,388
I was able to sequester myself
in the Ministry's Special Ward.

393
00:20:23,264 --> 00:20:26,183
There, I was safely beyond
Chairman Wong's reach.

394
00:20:26,267 --> 00:20:27,810
And your parents are safe, too,

395
00:20:27,893 --> 00:20:28,894
-by the way.
-[gasps]

396
00:20:29,603 --> 00:20:31,147
[grunts] Are they, really?

397
00:20:31,230 --> 00:20:33,399
-[MIHARU] Hmm.
-[Maki chuckles softly]

398
00:20:34,400 --> 00:20:36,152
The substance
contained in this spray

399
00:20:36,235 --> 00:20:38,154
can forcibly disconnect
a Sapotama

400
00:20:38,237 --> 00:20:40,114
from its owner's implant tag,

401
00:20:40,197 --> 00:20:41,490
which means...

402
00:20:41,574 --> 00:20:44,827
We can finally disconnect Asuka
from Albatusmon.

403
00:20:49,039 --> 00:20:50,082
Be careful.

404
00:20:50,166 --> 00:20:51,792
There's only one use left in it.

405
00:20:52,501 --> 00:20:56,172
Use it wisely and show me
that new world you promised.

406
00:20:56,839 --> 00:20:57,756
Mm.

407
00:20:59,425 --> 00:21:01,051
Where's Kawarazaki?

408
00:21:01,135 --> 00:21:03,429
We were told
the Ministry's been wiped out.

409
00:21:03,512 --> 00:21:05,723
♪

410
00:21:05,806 --> 00:21:07,099
[sighs]

411
00:21:08,184 --> 00:21:10,394
He wanted me to give you
this job request.

412
00:21:11,395 --> 00:21:12,980
-It's his last.
-[all gasp]

413
00:21:15,024 --> 00:21:17,818
Chairman Wong's fake Shangri-La.

414
00:21:19,862 --> 00:21:21,155
Tear it down.

415
00:21:22,823 --> 00:21:23,783
[ALL] Mm.

416
00:21:30,873 --> 00:21:33,959
Kyo, I won't lose my way again.

417
00:21:35,336 --> 00:21:36,420
Don't worry.

418
00:21:36,504 --> 00:21:38,964
I'll trust myself and my family.

419
00:21:40,090 --> 00:21:41,258
I'll see you later.

420
00:21:52,394 --> 00:21:53,270
Let's do it!

421
00:21:54,104 --> 00:21:56,106
[static hissing]

422
00:21:57,816 --> 00:21:59,777
Let's show 'em
what glitches can do.

423
00:22:01,403 --> 00:22:03,364
[♪ closing theme song playing]

424
00:23:01,005 --> 00:23:02,840
♪

425
00:23:02,923 --> 00:23:04,842
[TOMORO] I'm through hesitating.

426
00:23:04,925 --> 00:23:07,595
This time,
I swear I'll save Asuka!

427
00:23:07,678 --> 00:23:09,722
[GEKKOMON]
That's the spirit, you know?

428
00:23:09,805 --> 00:23:12,016
[REINA] Yeah, time to dig in!

429
00:23:12,099 --> 00:23:14,560
[MAKOTO] We have other allies
we can rely on, too.

430
00:23:14,643 --> 00:23:16,020
It's going to be okay.

431
00:23:16,103 --> 00:23:17,730
I know we'll succeed.

432
00:23:17,813 --> 00:23:18,814
[TOMORO] Yeah.

433
00:23:19,398 --> 00:23:21,275
We can't just let them
change the world as they please.

434
00:23:21,984 --> 00:23:24,028
Come on, everyone. Let's go!

435
00:23:24,987 --> 00:23:27,615
Next time on
Digimon Beatbreak...

436
00:23:27,698 --> 00:23:29,450
"The Ultimate Power."

